    3. Verify the assembled chain is a single connected component.
    4. Derive the input by extracting each group's columns, randomly shifting each group (except the first) back to its original unshifted row position, and inserting 1 blank separator column between groups.
    5. Validate that no group cells fall outside the 3-row grid after un-shifting (guaranteed by construction since groups originally fit before shifting).
